{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Behold, He spreads His light upon it</b> — upon the cloud, His rain. And some say: that rain is called \"light,\" because of the smaller luminary [the moon], for by its motions the rain comes about by the Creator's command. And the correct view in my eyes: <b>behold, He spreads His light upon it</b> is as its literal meaning, for the light spreads over the cloud." "<b>The roots of the sea He covered</b> — for by them [the waters] He judges peoples through light and rain."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:45.797767922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}